                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "84d3724f-f48d-4826-8301-ecd884cb9311",
                        "entry_id": "eb3dd7f5-73ce-3805-8b63-91310c02ea78",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "scrimped"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d300b793-40ff-305b-ab14-696f1ff5dd80",
                        "entry_id": "eb3dd7f5-73ce-3805-8b63-91310c02ea78",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make too small or short; to shortchange."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "sometimes",
                            "transitive",
                            "with-on"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ecfd6db-b127-4363-9911-7745f593012a",
                                "sense_id": "d300b793-40ff-305b-ab14-696f1ff5dd80",
                                "text": "to scrimp the pattern of a coat"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32bf45cb-87c2-4b09-bd57-8bc19063eaa1",
                                "sense_id": "d300b793-40ff-305b-ab14-696f1ff5dd80",
                                "text": "The company scrimped on the design so badly that it ended up defective."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df1f69f8-f4f8-3c8b-8077-3eb5ea65f5d3",
                        "entry_id": "eb3dd7f5-73ce-3805-8b63-91310c02ea78",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To limit or straiten; to put on short allowance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72c1e03a-fd7c-4e63-befd-804378f61be5",
                                "sense_id": "df1f69f8-f4f8-3c8b-8077-3eb5ea65f5d3",
                                "text": "For, as a general thing, the English merchant-ship scrimps her crew; but not so the English whaler."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be9b34ac-5e5e-4f18-a1e4-1565abe69e2b",
                                "sense_id": "df1f69f8-f4f8-3c8b-8077-3eb5ea65f5d3",
                                "text": "There the Master scrimps his haggard sempstress of her daily bread, / There a single sordid attic holds the living and the dead."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c75d771c-df38-32ea-92bc-d22fddb6b435",
                        "entry_id": "eb3dd7f5-73ce-3805-8b63-91310c02ea78",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be frugal, whether to a reasonable and wise extent or to a miserly and unwise extent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd88c0e2-00ff-49d2-a920-1e1c55cc3b29",
                                "sense_id": "c75d771c-df38-32ea-92bc-d22fddb6b435",
                                "text": "“Oh, Electra, jewel of women, darling of my heart, we are free at last, we roll in wealth, we need never scrimp again. It's a case for Veuve Cliquot!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3dfd6c7-7328-4a5d-b26e-c7b680e2d5c2",
                                "sense_id": "c75d771c-df38-32ea-92bc-d22fddb6b435",
                                "text": "They had to scrimp each month to afford it out of pocket."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
